Package: glmap
Title: High-Performance GPU Geospatial Mapping for 'sf' and 'terra'
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Bruno", "Tremblay", , "meztez@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mapbox", role = "cph", comment = "mapbox/earcut.hpp in src/earcut.h (ISC License)"),
    person("MapLibre contributors", role = "cph", comment = "MapLibre GL JS v4.7.1 in inst/htmlwidgets/lib/maplibre-gl (BSD-3-Clause License)"))
Description: A compact, high-performance WebGL2 and 'MapLibre GL' interactive
    mapping engine for R designed as a drop-in GPU replacement for 'leaflet'
    and 'leaflet.extras'. Bypasses 'htmlwidgets' JSON bottlenecks by streaming
    zero-copy 'GLMP' and 'GeoArrow' binary vertex/attribute buffers directly
    from C++17 to WebGL2 GPU shaders, with C++ 'mapbox/earcut' polygon hole
    triangulation, WebGL2 sprite texture atlases, screen-space marker clustering
    with spiderfy web expansion, zoom-level Level-of-Detail (LOD) cross-fading,
    in-memory spatial R-tree dynamic viewport slicing, 'DuckDB' out-of-core
    Parquet pushdown, live GPU fragment shaders for 'terra' rasters (0ms
    colormaps, hillshading, contrast stretching, and band math), full 'Shiny'
    proxy diffing, 'crosstalk' linked brushing, and a modular plugin architecture.
URL: https://meztez.github.io/glmap/, https://github.com/meztez/glmap
BugReports: https://github.com/meztez/glmap/issues
